{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For, in your eyes</b> — HaShem speaks with human beings; do not be astonished on account of the shift to plural person, and afterwards <b>in your eyes</b>, for such is the way of language. <b>Remember the days of old</b> — understand between them: your children, your wives, and your stranger. [n: 'between them' is obscure; possibly a textual difficulty in the parenthetical gloss on 'days of old']" "<b>And the meaning of 'like a day'</b> — perhaps you, O son of man, live a thousand years; thus they are <b>like yesterday, for it passes</b> having already passed, or <b>like a watch in the night</b>. And according to the plain sense, what reason to say <b>like yesterday</b>? It would have sufficed to say <b>a day</b>, and it is as though he lived a thousand years. And that which indicates the straightforward sense [of the matter] — my interpretation is that he says: <b>The days of our years among them are seventy years</b>, that they do not reach a thousand; and to interpret it of the generation of the flood is far-fetched."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 90, :notes {0 "The phrase בינו טפכם נשיכם וגרך is textually obscure; translated hyper-literally as 'understand between them: your children, your wives, and your stranger.' The connection to the verse is unclear and the passage may be corrupt.", 1 "The clause 'ואשר יורה יושר' (rendered 'that which indicates the straightforward sense') is textually uncertain; read here as referring to the peshat reading, though the phrasing is unusual."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:48.415302118Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}